LEVEL 8 → 9 — FINDING THE UNIQUE LINE WITH sort AND uniq


WHAT THIS LEVEL IS ABOUT : 

The file data.txt contains many repeated lines, and the password appears exactly once. This level introduces the Unix pipeline pattern — chaining commands so the output of one feeds the input of the next.


APPROACH : 

The solution required two commands chained together:
sort data.txt | uniq -u
sort arranges all lines alphabetically so duplicates become adjacent. uniq -u then prints only lines that appear exactly once.

Password obtained. [Not shared per OverTheWire rules]


KEY TAKEAWAY : 

uniq only compares adjacent lines — sorting first is not optional. This pipeline is a classic pattern applicable to log deduplication, frequency analysis, and identifying anomalous entries in large datasets.
